   "description": "Annual box plots show the distribution of differences between the primary deficit and the debt-stabilizing primary deficit across IDA countries from 2000 to 2025. Medians fall below zero in the mid-2000s and remain close to zero for most subsequent years. The highest upper whisker is in 2000, at approximately 27% of GDP, and the lowest lower whisker is in 2004, at approximately −27% of GDP.",
   "notes": "Sources: Original calculations based on data from country authorities.\nNote: Figure plots the distribution of historical differences between PD and DSPD as a percentage of GDP for the sample of IDA countries over the 2000–25 period. Both PD and DSPD are based on a three-year moving average to smooth out the business cycle. Each blue box represents the 25th (Q1) to 75th (Q3) percentile range, the line inside the box is the median, and the bottom and top whiskers are the 1.5 × IQR from Q1 and Q3, respectively. The larger the ΔDSPD, the larger the fiscal adjustment needed in the primary balance to ensure debt stabilization. DSPD = debt-stabilizing primary deficit; IQR = interquartile range; PD = primary deficit."
